<title>GERMANY: East German Feb adjusted jobless rises 9,000.</title>
<headline>East German Feb adjusted jobless rises 9,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Feb 97	 Jan 97	   Feb 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.414 million    1.393 million	1.310 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.298 million    1.289 million	1.222 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+9,000	+79,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		18.9 pct     18.7 pct	 17.5 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	78,198	 68,174	   117,000</p>
<p> Vacancies		   48,030	 45,017	   50,010</p>
<p> Change in number in work Dec 96	Nov 96</p>
<p>				-23,000	 -22,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
